%% # Spur with one analyzer and two sampling points (two needles). The NSD diverts the carrier, without stopping, into the
%% # spur. On its bottom stretch an antenna with a gate (antenna2) stops and reads
%% # every carrier: it can only let it go on (pass), towards Divert 1; it can't divert.
%% # On the up branch there are two standard diverts (d1, d2): every carrier
%% # stops there and is read, then it is diverted into the pit-lane of a needle or
%% # goes straight on, while the next carrier stops behind. A pit-lane leaves to the
%% # right, rises past the sampling point (needle on its right) and rejoins the up
%% # branch above its divert, so a carrier leaving needle 1 still stops at d2.
